{"id": "EUVD-2026-103742", "enisaUuid": "ea96d9bd-0563-3b62-a8cc-d3ffcf9eb35d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: alps: unregister DualPoint Stick input device on remove\n\nalps_input_configured() allocates a second input device (\"DualPoint\nStick\") with input_allocate_device() and registers it, but the\nalps_driver struct has no .remove handler and input2 is not tracked in\nhdev->inputs.  The default remove path (hid_hw_stop -> hidinput_disconnect)\nonly iterates hdev->inputs, so input2 is never unregistered and leaks\non every device removal.\n\nAdd a .remove handler that stops the device first (preventing URB\ncallbacks from touching input2 during teardown) and then unregisters\ninput2.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:16:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd9571812d02242b6bba2637fba924a78a5c6fa8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1170ebfba562b3938ff7749b2e42e4420f19436d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa4845a710ae9fee6a3831f5c338904cea77c3aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/978e801750c7b0859e87eae619f7d88fcd88333e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa9dde93e05a837645fdfd577eea71f0733f0694"], "aliases": ["GHSA-79qw-7wgp-r9xr", "CVE-2026-98502"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ff1a835-c976-3a00-8423-c1f5aeca3525", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2562756dde550901c224e3805102bdfc17e7d13a <978e801750c7b0859e87eae619f7d88fcd88333e"}, {"id": "210d56cd-aec6-34c8-84c7-a7b02e3b5b62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "36f95baf-d3a9-3924-a885-a358fc4e7350", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}, {"id": "5098140b-1c11-335d-ab7d-db53fb30341e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2562756dde550901c224e3805102bdfc17e7d13a <aa9dde93e05a837645fdfd577eea71f0733f0694"}, {"id": "63ef7d65-867f-3383-a91a-143fffee9d7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2562756dde550901c224e3805102bdfc17e7d13a <aa4845a710ae9fee6a3831f5c338904cea77c3aa"}, {"id": "71a0db48-aef3-3ae5-b2b7-97e39a771fe7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8336c260-631d-34e1-b7b5-d77e9a88f2bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2562756dde550901c224e3805102bdfc17e7d13a <bd9571812d02242b6bba2637fba924a78a5c6fa8"}, {"id": "84e905c5-0e97-3782-bf92-e36ecb0c6892", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2562756dde550901c224e3805102bdfc17e7d13a <1170ebfba562b3938ff7749b2e42e4420f19436d"}, {"id": "92bc01e3-7fc1-38e1-a4d6-a4636a8f5d78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "95eedd4a-6ec5-372a-b45d-e3d7d1d2b51a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "b0adee32-b327-37d8-9eaf-e3161e9f1e10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "e91ec9cd-67cb-3830-866c-aa0a8006c2d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "becd5e82-80b5-360f-bb1f-a900991ce6ea", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}